test_command=for t in tests/*.sh; do sh "$t"; done
id=bump471-01 result=green reason=13 tests/bump471_test.sh functions test_bump471_01_* all pass: VERSION reads 4.7.1 by agreement with the newest topmost entry (never a cross-change literal) with one trailing newline as its only content; exactly one dated '## [4.7.1] - 2026-09-13' heading sits above [4.7.0] above [4.6.0] (relative ordering only, the stacking lesson) with the Keep-a-Changelog preamble, in the file's entry style (### Changed, - ** bullets); the section-scoped extract pins the mirror clause stated exactly once in each of the four prompts, the four long sentences that became short lists (coder's closing-block bullet folded into ## Receipt, rejected_count=1 row, dedup guard, REJECTED.md entry), the triple negation replaced by the two-line table rule, the terminology unified (<change-slug> to <slug>, one form per concept), the Working-Root triplication documented as an editing rule in AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md and pinned by a test, the suites following with every diff-window assertion born gated on change_pending, the patch grade with its not-minor/not-major justification, and the [4.7.0]-down tail is byte-identical to git HEAD
id=bump471-02 result=green reason=5 tests/bump471_test.sh functions test_bump471_02_* all pass: the entry states agents/meta/* and install.sh byte-unchanged (the bump reaches installed copies only through the user's later ./install.sh --all) and no role creates the v4.7.1 tag; the install.sh/agents-meta-untouched and no-v4.7.1-tag guards are gated on change_pending and retire with a loud note once the bump commit lands; the gate's lifecycle is exercised on a throwaway scratch repo through all four states (off when clean, on while pending, retired when committed, never resurrected by a later legitimate bump) so the suite exits 0 in both the pending and the committed state; the suite's own source is pinned to read-only git invocations against the real repo (diff/show/tag -l) with every invocation carrying an explicit -C target
